  n<//         when 0. Therefore make sure it is glitch free.> u<291> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<292> f<1> l<154:1> el<154:58>
  n<//> u<292> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<293> f<1> l<155:1> el<155:3>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<293> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<294> f<1> l<156:1> el<156:58>
  n<//`define SYNC_CPU_EN> u<294> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<295> f<1> l<158:1> el<158:22>
  n<//`define SYNC_DBG_EN> u<295> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<296> f<1> l<159:1> el<159:22>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<296> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<297> f<1> l<162:1> el<162:58>
  n<// Peripheral Memory Space:> u<297> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<298> f<1> l<163:1> el<163:28>
  n<//-------------------------------------------------------> u<298> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<299> f<1> l<164:1> el<164:58>
  n<// The original MSP430 architecture map the peripherals> u<299> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<300> f<1> l<165:1> el<165:56>
  n<// from 0x0000 to 0x01FF (i.e. 512B of the memory space).> u<300> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<301> f<1> l<166:1> el<166:58>
  n<// The following defines allow you to expand this space> u<301> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<302> f<1> l<167:1> el<167:56>
  n<// up to 32 kB (i.e. from 0x0000 to 0x7fff).> u<302> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<5796> s<303> f<1> l<168:1> el<168:45>
